# Waqti Runtime — Multi-Token KVCache Correctness Harness

## Implemented API

Added:

```text
waqti::transformer::KVCache
waqti::attention::causal_attention(...)
waqti::transformer::forward_layer_cached(...)
waqti::sequence::forward(...)
```

`KVCache` stores one flat key/value array per layer. The layout is:

```text
keys[layer][position * kv_heads * head_dim + kv_head * head_dim + dimension]
values[layer][position * kv_heads * head_dim + kv_head * head_dim + dimension]
```

For this model:

```text
layers = 24
kv_heads = 2
head_dim = 64
repeat = 14 / 2 = 7
```

At position `p`, the attention routine receives exactly `p + 1` cached positions. Future positions are never visible.

## Real model sequences

Model: Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct Q4_K_M
Prompt tokens used: `[9707]`, `[9707, 11]`, `[9707, 11, 11, 11]`
Position: 0..N-1

```text
sequence_len=1
position 0: hidden_rms=15.5873 argmax=102610 logit=12.9598

sequence_len=2
position 0: hidden_rms=15.5873 argmax=102610 logit=12.9598
position 1: hidden_rms=13.4350 argmax=47865  logit=12.6375

sequence_len=4
position 0: hidden_rms=15.5873 argmax=102610 logit=12.9598
position 1: hidden_rms=13.4350 argmax=47865  logit=12.6375
position 2: hidden_rms=15.3332 argmax=8503   logit=11.4782
position 3: hidden_rms=15.2238 argmax=29032  logit=13.7792
```

The position-0 result is identical between the single-token and multi-token runs, proving no future-token leakage into position 0. Positions 1–3 produce distinct causal outputs.

